136
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:13,960
evaluations are specific measurement
tools, auditing is a systematic

137
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:17,919
process of safety verification. An audit
might employ multiple

138
00:09:17,919 --> 00:09:22,720
evaluations but also considers broader
factors like organizational processes,

139
00:09:22,799 --> 00:09:27,120
documentation and safety frameworks. For
example, when auditing a

140
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:30,120
model for deployment readiness, we don't
just run capability

141
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:34,440
evaluations. We also examine training
procedures, security measures, and

142
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,559
incident response plans. What types of
audits do we

143
00:09:37,559 --> 00:09:41,529
need? Different aspects of AI development
require different types

144
00:09:41,529 --> 00:09:46,490
of audits. 1. Training design audits.
These verify safety

145
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:51,370
considerations throughout the development
process. Before training begins, auditors

146
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:55,250
examine factors like compute usage plans,
training data content,

147
00:09:55,409 --> 00:09:59,690
and experiment design decisions. During
training, they monitor for

148
00:09:59,690 --> 00:10:04,129
concerning capabilities or behaviors. For
instance, training audits might

149
00:10:04,129 --> 00:10:07,309
look for indicators that scaling up model
size might

150
00:10:07,309 --> 00:10:14,070
lead to dangerous capabilities. Anthropic
2024 2. Security audits.

151
00:10:14,149 --> 00:10:18,230
These assess whether safety measures
remain effective under adversarial

152
00:10:18,230 --> 00:10:23,230
conditions. This includes technical
security like model isolation and

153
00:10:23,230 --> 00:10:28,149
access controls, and organizational
security like insider threat prevention.

154
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:34,080
3. Deployment audits these examine
specific deployment scenarios. They

155
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:37,639
consider questions like who will have
access? What affordances

156
00:10:37,639 --> 00:10:41,600
will be available? What safeguards are
needed? These audits

157
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:45,759
help determine whether deployment plans
adequately address potential risks.

158
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:49,919
For example, deployment audits might
assess both direct risks

159
00:10:49,919 --> 00:10:53,720
from model capabilities and potential
emergent risks from real

160
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:58,741
world usage patterns of those
capabilities. Apollo Research 2024

161
00:10:58,957 --> 00:11:04,409
4. Governance audits these look at
organizational safety infrastructure.

162
00:11:04,730 --> 00:11:09,169
They verify that companies have
appropriate processes, documentation
requirements,

163
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:14,090
and response protocols. This includes
reviewing incident response plans,

164
00:11:14,169 --> 00:11:19,929
oversight mechanisms, and transparency
practices. Chevalin et al. 2023.

